1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,090
Speaker 1: I have a recording from our product review.

2
00:00:02,530 --> 00:00:04,480
Speaker 1: Can we turn it into searchable captions?

3
00:00:04,870 --> 00:00:05,680
Speaker 2: Yes.

4
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:11,230
Speaker 2: First, we send the audio to Nemotron Transcribe on one H one hundred GPU.

5
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:14,480
Speaker 1: Will it tell us who is speaking and when each word starts?

6
00:00:14,870 --> 00:00:16,319
Speaker 2: That's the idea.

7
00:00:16,319 --> 00:00:21,118
Speaker 2: We ask for speaker tags and word timestamps, then check the result against the

8
00:00:21,118 --> 00:00:21,740
Speaker 2: recording.

9
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:22,878
Speaker 1: Great.

10
00:00:22,878 --> 00:00:27,590
Speaker 1: I can search for product review, jump to that moment, and export subtitle captions.

11
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:28,780
Speaker 2: Exactly.

12
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:33,810
Speaker 2: The transcript is useful, but a human should still review names and speaker changes.
